/* ============================================================================
   five-number-summary.epher -- min, Q1, median, Q3, max of a dataset

   The five-number summary of the ten exam scores in `d`: the minimum, the
   first quartile, the median, the third quartile and the maximum. Quartiles
   come from the builtin quartile(d, k), which follows the TI-83/84
   convention: the median of the lower half for Q1, of the upper half for
   Q3, and on an even count the median is the mean of the two middle values.

   Run it from a terminal:  epher "epher scripts/statistics/summary/five-number-summary.epher"
   In the REPL:             load epher scripts/statistics/summary/five-number-summary.epher
   Web/desktop:             paste the whole file into the entry, press Enter
   Everything also works line by line in the TUI.

   The one knob to edit is `d` below. Everything above the results section
   is machinery you can leave alone.
   ============================================================================ */

// ---- the knob -----------------------------------------------------------------
const d = {72, 85, 91, 64, 88, 79, 83, 95, 70, 86}   // exam scores, 10 students

// ---- the five numbers -----------------------------------------------------------
print("min:", min(d))              // smallest score
print("Q1:", quartile(d, 1))       // median of the lower half
print("median:", quartile(d, 2))   // the middle value (builtin median agrees)
print("Q3:", quartile(d, 3))       // median of the upper half
print("max:", max(d))              // largest score

/* ---- expected output ----
= {72, 85, 91, 64, 88, 79, 83, 95, 70, 86}
= min: 64
= Q1: 72
= median: 84
= Q3: 88
= max: 95
*/